Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(detection): CLO-129 implement env.location_mock
 probe (rank 39)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Adds LocationMockProbe.kt and LocationMockProbeTest.kt under
agents/detection/src/probes/env/ following the TimeSpoofingProbe
pattern (Probe interface, KDoc, evidence emission).

Detection strategy — four independent signals, score is max:

  S1  Location.isFromMockProvider() = true        score 1.00
      Strongest evidence: the active fix itself is flagged mocked.

  S2  Settings.Secure.mock_location = "1"         score 0.85
      Legacy ALLOW_MOCK_LOCATION developer toggle (API <=22).

  S3  >=1 pkg holds ACCESS_MOCK_LOCATION           score 0.70 base,
                                                   +0.10/pkg, capped 1.0
      Reverse-direction successor to S2 from API 23.

  S4  Reverse-geocoder anomaly                    score 0.65
      Reverse-geocoding the last fix returns no/inconsistent address
      vs. the reported coordinates. Surfaced via Settings.Secure
      sentinel 'location.geocoder_anomaly'; production wrapper performs
      the Geocoder.getFromLocation() call.

Confidence: 0.99 if S1, 0.90 if any of S2/S3/S4, 0.95 on clean true-negative.

Acceptance (CI-only):
  cmd: gradle :detection:test --tests LocationMockProbeTest
  expect_exit: 0
  expect: 4 test cases — clean / isFromMockProvider=true /
          allowMockLocation setting=1 / geocoder-anomaly

Each of the four required acceptance cases is implemented as a separate
@Test isolating one signal at a time with the others clean. Three
additional tests exercise S3 (package permissions), signal priority
(S1 beats S2/S3/S4), and probe metadata (id + rank match inventory).

The gitleaks config copy under docs/super-action/W6/.git-hooks/ is
restored from the existing untracked file in the parent worktree so the
pre-commit secrets scan can run; identical contents to the file already
in use across other branches.

Refs: CLO-129, inventory rank 39 (env.location_mock)

